question:
For what negative value of $k$ is there exactly one solution to the system of equations \begin{align*}
y &= 2x^2 + kx + 6 \\
y &= -x + 4?
\end{align*}

Let $f$ be defined by  \[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
3-x & \text{ if } x \leq 3, \\
-x^3+2x^2+3x & \text{ if } x>3.
\end{array}
\right.\]Calculate $f^{-1}(0)+f^{-1}(6)$.

